# The modules that the kernel of hd-kernel-vm keeps of the config of Debian; make localmodconfig
# turns off every other module. What the config of Debian builds into the kernel stays. A line is
# one of:
#
#   <dir>/    every module of the directory <dir> of the kernel tree and of those below it
#   !<dir>/   none of the directory <dir> and of those below it, of a directory kept above
#   <module>  the module of that name, as lsmod prints it; the build stops when the kernel has no
#             module of that name, as a module or built in
#
# Everything but the drivers stays: file systems, network protocols and netfilter, crypto, and
# the kvm of the processor for vms in the vm. Of the drivers only those of the hardware that
# QEMU emulates for a KVM vm stay, and the drivers of software that are not hardware.

# Everything but the drivers, and not the protocols of hardware that a vm has not.
